Open Visual Studio Code and create a new Flutter project.
Create an assets folder inside the project.
Create an images folder inside the assets folder.
Add three images representing Ooty, Kodaikanal and Kanyakumari.
Open the pubspec.yaml file and configure the image assets path.
Save the file and execute flutter pub get to load the assets.
Open main.dart and import the Flutter Material package.
Create a MaterialApp and a Scaffold with an AppBar titled Tamil Nadu Tourism Gallery.
Use GridView.count() with crossAxisCount: 2 to arrange the images in two columns.
Use Image.asset() to display the tourist destination images and Text() to display their names.
Run the application using flutter run.
Verify that all three images are displayed properly with their destination names.
